faqHeading: Frequently asked questions
faq:
  - q: What does HelioLattice cover?
    a: Enquiries and pipeline, survey and quotation, delivery checklist, materials and stock, payments and expenses, AMC and service, reports, a partner portal and roles and access control.
  - q: Who is it for?
    a: Rooftop solar installers and EPC companies in India, from residential installers to commercial and channel-led businesses.
  - q: Does it work for residential and commercial projects?
    a: Yes. Delivery stages, documents and utility or subsidy steps are configured per type of job.
  - q: Can I control who sees what?
    a: Yes. There are 269 permissions across 26 areas, custom roles, data scopes and hidden internal costing.
  - q: Can my channel partners use it?
    a: Yes. Partners sign in to a separate portal to submit leads, follow their status and view commission.
  - q: Can surveyors use it on a phone?
    a: Yes. The survey runs in a mobile browser and captures location, details and categorised photos.
  - q: Does it handle AMC and service after installation?
    a: Yes. AMC invoices and receipts, support tickets, service costs, warranty replacements and vendor recovery sit on the customer's record.
  - q: Does it work with Tally?
    a: Approved claims export to Tally XML, Tally JSON and Excel.
  - q: Do you support WhatsApp?
    a: WhatsApp conversations are logged on enquiries, and messaging, internal notification bots and customer bots are set up during implementation.
  - q: How is it priced?
    a: One yearly plan with every module, plus a one-time implementation fee sized to your scope. Both are quoted in writing after a demo.
  - q: How does implementation work?
    a: We study your business, configure stages, roles and catalogue, set up your starting data and train your team.
  - q: How do I get started?
    a: Book a demo and bring a few open jobs.
